{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": [
    "THE ROUTE TABLE (wave 13, function budget).",
    "",
    "One machine-readable source of truth for every PUBLIC API URL of the Vercel",
    "tree. Three consumers read it, so it can never disagree with itself:",
    "",
    "  1. the two entry points (api/portal.ts, api/admin.ts) - they map a route",
    "     to a handler module;",
    "  2. site/scripts/check-api-routes.mjs - it verifies that every called URL",
    "     is served and that the handler module behind it exists;",
    "  3. site/scripts/dev-portal.js - the local dev server serves the SAME table",
    "     the deployed target serves, instead of matching by prefix.",
    "",
    "families:   one entry point serves several public URLs. The entry file is a",
    "            Vercel FUNCTION (one file = one function = one Hobby slot).",
    "            vercel.json rewrites every route of a family to that entry",
    "            point with the ORIGINAL public path in the __imk_route query",
    "            parameter.",
    "standalone: a public URL that keeps its own function file (a query-bearing",
    "            URL or a security-sensitive family).",
    "handlers:   handler module name -> the file that implements it.",
    "",
    "The '*' pattern is ONE dynamic segment - the same shape as the platform's",
    "[id].ts route. There is no catch-all."
  ],
  "families": {
    "/api/portal": {
      "entry": "api/portal.ts",
      "routes": {
        "/api/portal/comments": "portal-comments",
        "/api/portal/invites": "portal-invites",
        "/api/portal/plan-items": "portal-plan-items",
        "/api/portal/plan-items/*": "portal-plan-items",
        "/api/portal/projects": "portal-projects",
        "/api/portal/projects/*": "portal-projects",
        "/api/portal/session": "portal-session",
        "/api/portal/testimonials": "portal-testimonials",
        "/api/portal/updates": "portal-updates"
      }
    },
    "/api/admin": {
      "entry": "api/admin.ts",
      "routes": {
        "/api/admin/reviews": "admin-reviews",
        "/api/admin/session": "admin-session"
      }
    }
  },
  "standalone": {
    "/api/contact": { "entry": "api/contact.ts", "handler": "contact" },
    "/api/moderate/review": { "entry": "api/moderate/review.ts", "handler": "moderate" },
    "/api/portal/auth/request-link": {
      "entry": "api/portal/auth/request-link.ts",
      "handler": "portal-auth"
    },
    "/api/portal/auth/verify": {
      "entry": "api/portal/auth/verify.ts",
      "handler": "portal-auth"
    },
    "/api/portal/auth/logout": {
      "entry": "api/portal/auth/logout.ts",
      "handler": "portal-auth"
    }
  },
  "handlers": {
    "contact": "api/contact.ts",
    "moderate": "api/moderate/review.ts",
    "portal-auth": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-auth.ts",
    "portal-comments": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-comments.ts",
    "portal-invites": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-invites.ts",
    "portal-plan-items": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-plan-items.ts",
    "portal-projects": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-projects.ts",
    "portal-session": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-session.ts",
    "portal-testimonials": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-testimonials.ts",
    "portal-updates": "site/shared/portal-handlers/portal-updates.ts",
    "admin-reviews": "site/shared/portal-handlers/admin-reviews.ts",
    "admin-session": "site/shared/portal-handlers/admin-session.ts"
  }
}
